The base side length of the first pyramid is $\blueD{\sqrt{\dfrac{6V}{h}}}$.

Let's take $\sqrt{\dfrac{6\goldD V}{h}}$ and replace $\goldD V$ with $\goldD{9V}$:

$\begin{align}
\sqrt{\dfrac{6(\goldD{9V})}{h}}&=\sqrt{\dfrac{9\cdot 6V}{h}}
\\\\
&=\sqrt9\cdot\sqrt{\dfrac{6V}{h}}
\\\\
&=3\left(\blueD{\sqrt{\dfrac{6V}{h}}}\right)
\end{align}$

We started with an expression where $V$ is increased by a factor of $9$ and ended with the overall expression increased by a factor of $3$.
